# Game Detail Page — Code & UI Review
`src/app/[game]/page.tsx`

---

## 🔴 Bugs / Broken Things

### 1. `<a>` wrapping `<button>` — invalid HTML
```tsx
// Current (invalid)
<a href={p?.releaseDetails?.download} target="_blank">
  <button>Download for Windows</button>
</a>
```
Interactive elements must not be nested. This breaks keyboard navigation and screen readers.  
**Fix:** Make the `<a>` the styled element itself, or use `router.push` on a `<button>`.

---

### 2. Download URL is `undefined` when game has no desktop build
`p?.releaseDetails?.download` can be `undefined`. When it is, the `<a>` renders with `href={undefined}`, which makes it a dead no-op link — no visual feedback to the user.

---

### 3. `useRouter` is imported but never used
`router` is declared but no code path calls it. Dead import.

---

### 4. `SlideShow` is imported but never rendered
`SlideShow` is imported at the top of the file but removed from the JSX. Dead import creating a bundle weight.

---

### 5. `ExternalLink` icon imported but never used
Same issue — dead import from `lucide-react`.

---

### 6. Body scroll lock is never cleaned up on unmount
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  document.body.classList.toggle("overflow-hidden", showIfram);
}, [showIfram]);
```
If the component unmounts while `showIfram === true` (e.g. user navigates away via back button), `overflow-hidden` stays on `<body>` forever — page stays un-scrollable.  
**Fix:** Add a cleanup function that removes the class.

---

### 7. `brandColor` contains hover/text classes — splitting by `" "[0]` is fragile
```tsx
product.brandColor?.split(" ")[0] // e.g. "bg-violet-600"
```
This assumes the format is always `bg-X hover:bg-Y text-Z`. If any game's `brandColor` changes order, the accent bar silently gets the wrong colour.

---

## 🟡 UX / Usability Issues

### 8. No "back" navigation
There is no breadcrumb or back button. Users must rely on the browser back button. If they arrived from a deep link, back goes to the browser history — not the game library.

### 9. No game screenshot / gallery section
`SlideShow` was built for this exact purpose and then commented out. The page has a cover banner but no in-game screenshots, leaving a large empty visual gap between the cover and the info card.

### 10. The iframe overlay has no loading indicator
Clicking "Play Now" fires the iframe immediately with no spinner. The game can take 2–5 seconds to load — the user sees a blank black screen.

### 11. No Escape key handler for the iframe overlay
Common UX expectation: pressing `Escape` should close the fullscreen game. Currently only the close button works.

### 12. Close button is hard to hit — only 36×36px and too close to navbar
`top-20 right-5` puts it 80px from the top. On mobile this overlaps the Navbar area and is too small (< 44px touch target).

### 13. Play count, avg time, and difficulty are not shown on the detail page
The game card shows these stats. The detail page strips them out — users lose context after clicking through.

### 14. No "Related Games" or "More Games" section
After viewing a game, there is no path forward. Users have to scroll all the way back to the game grid. A "Play More Games" row at the bottom would improve session depth.

### 15. "Not Found" state still renders `<Navbar>` incorrectly
```tsx
if (!product) {
  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen flex items-center ...">
      <Navbar />         // ← inside a centered flex container
      <p>Game not found.</p>
    </div>
  );
}
```
The Navbar is inside the centered `div`, so it renders in the middle of the page rather than at the top.

---

## 🟢 Code Quality

### 16. `showIfram` typo — should be `showIframe`
Minor but it's a typo that exists in 8+ places.

### 17. `specRows` is defined inside the component on every render
It doesn't close over any state — it's a pure function that should be extracted outside the component or memoised.

### 18. Star rating logic is duplicated
The same `[1,2,3,4,5].map(...)` star-rendering block appears in both `GameCard.tsx` and this page. Should be a shared `<StarRow>` component (already exists in `GameCard` — extract it to a separate file).

### 19. `product.type` has no TypeScript type — uses `any`
```tsx
product.type?.map((t: { text: string; color: string }, i: number) => ...)
```
The inline type cast is necessary because `type: any` in `constants.ts`. Should be `type Tag[]` where `Tag = { text: string; color: string }`.

---

